{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Therefore by this the iniquity of Jacob is atoned.</b> The meaning is that evil will not come upon him, for the iniquity of Jacob is evil; and the meaning is that the decree would have been annulled, had they abolished idolatry:" "<b>Remove.</b> Infinitive." "<b>Altar.</b> Of the Baalim." "<b>Lime.</b> Like סיד [lime]." "<b>Shattered.</b> As in 'כלי יוצר תנפצם' [like a potter's vessel you shall shatter them]; broken." "<b>They shall not rise.</b> They shall stand."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:25.439952699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}